1
00:00:00,225 --> 00:00:03,092
For a thousand years, geniuses thought your eyes shoot lasers.

2
00:00:03,369 --> 00:00:04,342
Behold my vision beams!

3
00:00:04,675 --> 00:00:07,213
Then Cairo polymath Ibn al-Haytham stepped into total darkness.

4
00:00:07,475 --> 00:00:09,266
If eyes shoot light, why can't you see now?

5
00:00:09,725 --> 00:00:14,895
Through one tiny pinhole, candle rays raced straight, crossed over, and projected the flame...

6
00:00:15,574 --> 00:00:17,280
Wait—why is it upside down?!

7
00:00:17,525 --> 00:00:20,110
Because light enters your eye—it never shoots out!

8
00:00:20,625 --> 00:00:24,225
He built the Camera Obscura—and unlocked human vision.

9
00:00:25,575 --> 00:00:29,076
Every phone camera today? Still inside his dark room.
